    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0152" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5804</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Ministry of Foreign
                            Affairs to the Chinese
                        Legation</hi><anchor n="67" xml:id="d45-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-10">January 10, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Spokesman of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, in an interview to-day,
                    categorically denied the Tokyo report that in accordance with Chinese proposals
                    negotiations will open shortly for a settlement of the Shanhaikwan affair and
                    that General Ho Chu-Kuo will represent Marshal Chang Hsiao-Liang in this coming
                    negotiation.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d45-f1" n="67" type="source" xml:id="d45-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of telegram transmitted to the Department by the Chinese Legation on January
                    11.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
